+### 4.3 list_conversations
+
+Asks the server for the authenticated user's conversation list. No `userId` field is accepted from the frame; the server always reads the user identity from the upgrade auth. `limit` is an optional integer 1–200 bounding the page. `before` is an optional cursor carrying both `updatedAt` (a string `Date.parse` accepts) and `sessionId`; either half alone is `INVALID_MESSAGE`. `transport.history` must be enabled or the server answers `UNSUPPORTED`; a store with no `listFor` also answers `UNSUPPORTED`. The frame is accepted by `validateMessage` whether or not the feature is enabled — the handler is what refuses it, not the validator ([validated by: conversation list delivery](../../src/transport/ws/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts)).
+
+| Field    | Type   | Required | Description                                      |
+| -------- | ------ | -------- | ------------------------------------------------ |
+| `type`   | string | Yes      | `"list_conversations"`                           |
+| `limit`  | number | No       | Maximum summaries to return; integer 1–200       |
+| `before` | object | No       | Cursor: `{updatedAt: string, sessionId: string}` |
 
