+### 5.9 conversation_list
+
+Sent in response to a `list_conversations` frame when `transport.history` is enabled and the store implements `listFor`. It is never sent unsolicited. It carries one authenticated user's own conversation metadata and no conversation content; the user id is taken from the connection, never from the frame. `transport.history` is the deployer's decision to make a user's history reachable from the client.
+
+| Field           | Type                  | Description                      |
+| --------------- | --------------------- | -------------------------------- |
+| `type`          | string                | `"conversation_list"`            |
+| `conversations` | ConversationSummary[] | Summaries, newest activity first |
+
+`ConversationSummary` fields:
+
+| Field        | Type   | Description                           |
+| ------------ | ------ | ------------------------------------- |
+| `sessionId`  | string | The conversation's id                 |
+| `createdAt`  | string | ISO 8601 creation time                |
+| `updatedAt`  | string | ISO 8601 time of latest activity      |
+| `entryCount` | number | Number of entries in the conversation |
+
+`Date` does not survive `JSON.stringify` as a `Date`, so the protocol carries ISO strings. `conversation_list` is never followed by `stream_end` — it is not a turn.
+
